# Contributing to IgnisTrace

Thank you for your interest in contributing to **IgnisTrace**! Whether you are optimizing on-device Edge AI models, refining firmware logic for the dual-core architecture, or testing hardware power efficiency, we welcome your inputs.

---

## Code of Conduct

By participating in this project, you agree to maintain a respectful, constructive, and collaborative environment for all contributors. Please keep discussions focused on constructive technical feedback and problem-solving.

---

## How You Can Contribute

We welcome contributions across several key areas:

* **Embedded Firmware (C/C++):** Optimizing the STM32 MCU task scheduler, I2C sensor sampling routines, or dual-axis servo raster scanning algorithms[span_0](start_span)[span_0](end_span).
* **Edge AI & Machine Learning:** Training, quantizing, and tuning 1D ConvNet / MobileNet audio classification models for chainsaw and fire-crackle detection in noisy environment profiles.
* **Hardware & Circuit Engineering:** Refining power distribution circuits, PCB layouts, antenna designs, or IP65-rated ePTFE enclosure models.
* **Documentation & Testing:** Expanding setup guides, documenting pinout changes, or submitting field verification test logs.

